.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-mirror 1  "taur-mirror " 
.SH NAME
taur\-mirror \- Copy selected recipes from an AUR\-style Git source. Not a pacman binary repository and not an operator or Arch verification. Nothing is fetched until `sync`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur mirror\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy selected recipes from an AUR\-style Git source. Not a pacman binary repository and not an operator or Arch verification. Nothing is fetched until `sync`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
taur\-mirror\-add(1)
Add a recipe Git base URL. TAUR fetches `{url}/{pkgbase}.git`. Refuses pacman database URLs, credentials, and non\-https public schemes
.TP
taur\-mirror\-list(1)
List configured recipe mirrors
.TP
taur\-mirror\-select(1)
Choose package bases to copy. Does not fetch them
.TP
taur\-mirror\-unselect(1)
Stop updating a package. The last copy stays until `drop`
.TP
taur\-mirror\-sync(1)
Fetch selected packages. A missing upstream or a rejected package keeps the last copy
.TP
taur\-mirror\-status(1)
Show selection, revision, and whether a copy is stale
.TP
taur\-mirror\-remove(1)
Remove the source after its packages have been dropped
.TP
taur\-mirror\-drop(1)
Delete one package that this mirror stored. A locally maintained package is refused
.TP
taur\-mirror\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (database, git repos, outbox, SSH host key). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
